  "src.title": "Where every number comes from", "build.title": "How it is built", "build.txt": "A trip search over the published timetable (a connection scan), run in your browser; Python scripts that turn schedules, Census tables and crash records into small files; a model for walking risk tested on later years. Nothing runs on a server. Checks: the trip search is compared with 129 real timetable trips in both directions, and two separate implementations of the bus-coverage numbers agree on 720 of 720 spot checks.",
  "empabout.title": "The problem at real workplaces", "empabout.lead": "We checked {n} of the county's biggest employers against the bus schedule. At 11 PM on a weekday, {a} have a bus within a 5-minute walk. At 5 AM, {b} do.",
